  "notes": [
    "earthquake history contamination: the fold windows contain no quake rows, every window starts after 2016-05-15, the end of the earthquake_decay tail",
    "the per-store pre-opening training mask means store 52 trains on zero windows and stores 20, 21, 22, 29, 36, 42 and 53 train only from their own opening dates",
    "absence of local_test: this track never reads, scores or tunes on it; the freeze scores it once, on S1's side",
    "percentage-error metric excluded at 35.2% zeros in train+valid",
    "calendar encoding decision: the day-of-week and day-of-year sine and cosine features are calendar-built and future-known by design",
    "rolling-origin protocol: the three 16-day windows at the tail of valid are each predicted from a history that stops at its origin",
    "the fold metrics are re-predicted from the checkpoints, one history per fold, with the history stopping at each fold's origin",
    "the fold rows are the valid rows inside each window: 28,512 per fold and 85,536 pooled over the three",
    "the fold re-prediction ran on mps; the checkpoints are device-neutral and were trained on the device recorded in shared_config.device",
    "the fold SCORING path does not apply the training mask: S1's contract says scoring paths never see fit_rows, and the masked history would leave store 52 without a lookback and drop the fold from the pinned 28,512 rows",
    "the runtime_tradeoff benchmark was measured on the machine that re-scored the folds, one device entry per device it could run, each carrying its own torch version; the headline runs used the device in shared_config.device (cuda)",
    "the git_sha names the commit this artifact was generated on top of, because a commit cannot carry its own sha",
    "the three folds were re-predicted in 1.2 s in total on mps",
    "comparison.best_deep_full_grid_rmsle is the RMSLE of the three tail folds scored jointly (85,536 rows), the number S3's pooled block carries, so the two sides are comparable"
  ]
